A||||11||REDHOTT88||Is $800.00 a good price for a running Fiero? ||||5||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||11-29-2001||07:33 PM||||I just called a classified about an 1986 Silver 2m6 4 speed w/120,000 miles. He's asking $800.00  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> The guy doesn't seem like a Fiero enthusiast. He has several other trucks and cars for sale.<P>I know its hard to judge a car without seeing it, but he told me paint is good, no scratches, runs good and all accessories are working. (Although the headliner is saggy) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I only really know about 1988 Formulas, so I'm kinda at a loss on expertise on the earlier versions.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>Any input would be appreciated, I'm going to look at it tommorrow!<P>Thanks in advance!!!<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed<BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red & shiny all over - with all the options!)</FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-29-2001||07:49 PM||||Check it out good and take it for a drive. If everything is to your liking, GO FOR IT!<BR>$800.00 for a running, driving and working accessories for an 86 2M6 (SE) is a nice price. I'd buy it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||11-29-2001||07:57 PM||||A sagging headliner is <I>nothing</I> to worry about.  A running 6-cylinder Fiero for $800 sounds pretty good to me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||11-29-2001||07:57 PM||||Thanks alot!!<P> I'm heading out for about an hour.. go ahead post, I'll check back later! <P> I also wanted to ask if the 86's came with spoilers like the Formulas,or plain, or what?<P>The seller told me it didn't have a spoiler when I asked him. But he didn't act like it was missing.<P>Are all 86 2m6's, SE's?<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brandon86SE||11-29-2001||08:26 PM||||86 2M6's could be either a GT or a SE.  The SE's had the spoiler as an option, as well as luggage rack (like mine), or bare.  The GT's came standard with 'em, but could be requested without.  BTW, 4speeds are a lot of fun!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||11-29-2001||08:33 PM||||There was a guy in my area who was selling a 1988 GT that 'needs work' for $500 or best offer.  By the time I got to calling him (2 days after the ad ran), the car had already sold.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||11-29-2001||08:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>86 2M6's could be either a GT or a SE.</B><P>Not exactly true.  The 2M6 nomenclature was only used on the SE models.....2M6 doesn't appear anywhere on a GT.   <P><BR><B>The SE's had the spoiler as an option, as well as luggage rack (like mine), or bare.  The GT's came standard with 'em, but could be requested without.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope.  The spoiler was only standard on '84 Indy's and '88 Formulas.  They were options on all '85-'88 GT's, '86-'87 SE's and '88 coupes (as part of the WO2 option package).<P>I believe the price of a spoiler (at least in '88) was $369.<P>  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||REDHOTT88||11-29-2001||10:13 PM||||Thanks for the input...<P>Now stop fighting kids!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||11-29-2001||10:59 PM||||Before you buy the 2M6, pull back the carpeting on the sides of the trunk, and make sure it's not rusted out. <BR>If it's in decent shape and not rusted out, $800 sounds like a good price to me.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||11-29-2001||11:22 PM||||LISTEN TO RAYDAR!!<P>car can look and run great, but be completely rusted away underneath.. I just bought a project car last weekend, with hopes of restoring it. The seller told me it was probably only good for parts, and after hearing what it's gonna cost me to fix it, he was right. I'm disappointed, but I knew what I was getting into, and was well warned.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||4
